  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 118678,
  "projectUrl": "https://app.assently.com/api/assentlyclient",
  "published": "2026-11-25T22:34:43.107Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Fix: GET requests no longer send a Content-Type header. On .NET Core and .NET 5 and later, that header also added \"Content-Length: 0\", and load balancers with strict HTTP checks rejected the request with HTTP 400.\n\t\t- Fix: an enum value that this version does not know, for example a new case status, no longer makes GetCase, FindCases, FindTemplates or CallbackHelper.BindCaseEvent throw. The value is read as a number that is not a named member of the enum. If you send it back, for example with UpdateCase or as a FindCases filter, the client throws before it sends the request.\n\t\t- Fix: you can use one AssentlyClient from several threads at the same time, for example as a singleton in dependency injection. Before, parallel calls failed with \"WebClient does not support concurrent I/O operations\".\n\t\t- The User-Agent header now also names the .NET runtime, for example \".NET 8.0.11\".\n\t\t- The package now has a README, complete XML documentation and embedded debug symbols, so stack traces from the client show file and line numbers.\n\t\t- The package is licensed under the MIT license. Earlier versions had an empty license file.\n\t\t- Requires Newtonsoft.Json 13.0.4 or later.\n\t\t- netstandard2.0: no longer depends on the System.Net.Http, System.Net.WebHeaderCollection and System.Collections.Specialized packages.\n\t\t- If you update from 6.0.3 or older: CaseEvent has the values ApprovalAdded, RejectionAdded and FinalApproval (added in 6.0.4). Version 6.0.3 throws when it receives them.",
